<title>USA: Spieker Properties Inc Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Spieker Properties Inc Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>							 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								    March 31</p>
<p>							    1997	 1996</p>
<p>    Revenues					  $66,417   $45,315</p>
<p>Income from operations before</p>
<p>disposal of real estate properties</p>
<p>     and minority interests		   $ 23,812   $ 14,979</p>
<p>Net income available to</p>
<p>     Common Stockholders (a)		  $ 19,121     $9,859</p>
<p>    Average Common Stock shares outstanding 44,301     31,336</p>
<p>Net income per share available</p>
<p>     to Common Stockholders (b)		    $.43	$.31</p>
<p>    Funds from Operations			 $31,970   $20,839</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding (fully diluted)</p>
<p>							   52,558    39,105</p>
<p>    Funds from Operations per share (c)	  $.61	$.53</p>
<p>    Occupancy rate				    96.0%     96.7%</p>
<p>(a)  Net income after minority interests, less dividends</p>
<p>on Series A and Series B Preferred Stock.</p>
<p>(b)  Calculated based on average Common Stock shares</p>
<p>outstanding, assuming conversion of Class B Common Stock, Class C Common Stock and Common Stock Equivalents.</p>
<p>(c)  Calculated based on average shares outstanding, assuming conversion of Series A Preferred Stock, Class B Common Stock, Class C Common Stock, Common Stock Equivalents and all Partnership Units outstanding.</p>
